{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BraidsAndKnots.QCasimirUnique","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BraidsAndKnots.QCasimirUnique","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CasimirShared"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QCasimir.not_unique_up_to_scalar_unconstrained","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QCasimir.not_unique_up_to_scalar_unconstrained","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir-unique.lean#L102-L116","doc":"**The former axiom is false**: in `R_q × R_q` the central element\n`(1, 0)` is not the Casimir plus a scalar. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:q-casimir-unique","label":"prop:q-casimir-unique","md":"quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir-unique.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QCasimir.dDiag","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QCasimir.dDiag","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir-unique.lean#L84-L100","doc":"Casimir data on `QCasimir.qsDiag`, with `ι` the diagonal map. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QCasimir.qsDiag","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QCasimir.qsDiag","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir-unique.lean#L71-L82","doc":"The diagonal algebra `R_q × R_q` with `q = 2`, `E = F = 0`,\n`K = K⁻¹ = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.charZero_R_q_casimirUnique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.charZero_R_q_casimirUnique","kind":"instance","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir-unique.lean#L53-L55","doc":"`R_q = ℚ(q)` has characteristic zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CasimirScalarEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CasimirScalarEquiv","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir-unique.lean#L42-L51","doc":"**Differ by a scalar multiple of the identity.**  Two algebra elements\n`x y : qs.Algebra` are *scalar-equivalent* when `y = x + ι(r) · 1` for\nsome ground-ring scalar `r ∈ R_q` embedded via a central embedding `ι`.\nThis is the precise meaning of the narrative's \"differ by a scalar\nmultiple of the identity\" (`R_q`-scalars sit in the centre, so the shift\n`C'_q = C_q + ι(r)·1` exhausts the admissible re-normalisations). ","signatureChunk":0}]}